  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">PIMS-9581_01001914_CRI_PPG_Sustainable livestock in the Arenal-North Huetar Conservation Area (ACAHN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">This project aims to promote a regenerative livestock production model that contributes to ecosystem restoration including biodiversity conservation. This offers an alternative solution to conventional and unsustainable agricultural practices in the region, contributing to increase forest cover within private lands and the implementation of low-carbon and nature-positive practices. This model also seeks to reduce conflict with jaguars, facilitates biodiversity conservation through biological corridors, and maintains rural sustainable livelihoods. This will be a child project of the GEF-8 Food Systems Integrated Program</narrative>
  </description>
